  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n## Scenario\n\nThere's a top level frame A hosting an iframe B with the policy `focus-without-user-activation` denied. A calls `element_b.focus()` where `element_b` is an element in iframe B.\n\n(A has the policy allowed)\n\n## Desired outcome\n\n`element_b` gets focused.\n\n## Current outcome\n\nWith the current specs, [allow focus steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#allow-focus-steps) returns `false` since in step 1 it looks at `target` to see if it's got the policy allowed.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nLook at the \"caller\" frame's policy allowance (in this case A) instead of the target.\n\nThis would also align with the resolution from TPAC 2024 that \"Focus delegation should also be allowed (allow parent frame programmatically set focus into child iframe)\"\nhttps://github.com/w3c/webappsec-permissions-policy/issues/273#issuecomment-2384287101",
